GPU families.  Run in BVT on GPU families only which support dEQP (and are known to pass gles2.functional.hasty shards).  Also update broadwell expectations. Many more tests should be passing and running now.  BUG=510208 TEST=None.  Change-Id: Ifb3e73981f864912430de3f9005612829f7a3d19 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304626 Commit-Ready: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304626" owner_email="ihf@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/26/304626/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifff116a44b270c691c9250c6da90863cad63f9a7" commit="d359a052a311d54f540742f76902dfc1ca55dae3" commit_message="cbuildbot: Truly support custom artifacts.json  The support for customized archive list through &lt;overlay&gt;/scripts/artifacts.json in current implementation is fictitious, for various reasons:  * BuildAndArchiveAllImages asserts that base image is to be archived if a config   requests a recovery image. This requirement is very likely to be overlooked   when people write their artifacts.json, and it's config specific while   artifacts.json applies to all configs for a board. So it's better to just do   the right thing (archive the base image) instead of asserting users to   remember everything. * BuildAndArchiveAllImages relies on a second call to LoadArtifactsList to   add the recovery image in the archive list. This bases on a false assumption   that there's not an artifacts.json found because if there is, the second call   will get whatever the first call gets. * commands.BuildStandaloneArchive does nothing when 'archive' is omitted in   artifacts.json, whereas it should have at least copied the input from   image_dir to archive_dir because the GS uploader only looks for things in   archive_dir.  BUG=chromium:540049 TEST=Trybot run with rambi-release and a config that has a custom artifacts.json  Change-Id: Ifff116a44b270c691c9250c6da90863cad63f9a7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304324 Commit-Ready: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Wang &lt;wonderfly@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304324" owner_email="wonderfly@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/24/304324/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I53d659a7962a2137fd922585881a189f8ac8e254" commit="5a361cf014bb9368e996b5baa3dca81152c85d25" commit_message="linux-firmware: Add firmware patch for Intel Bluetooth 7265 (D1)  This patch adds the firmware patch for Intel Bluetooth 7265 (D1) also known as Intel StP D1.  D1 Patch Version: 9  Release Version: 153.1  Signed-off-by: Tedd Ho-Jeong An &lt;tedd.an@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kyle McMartin &lt;kyle@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit d82d3c1e5eddb811a38513a7e5b33202773f0fff) Signed-off-by: Tedd Ho-Jeong An &lt;tedd.an@intel.com&gt;  Conflicts:  WHENCE  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46259 TEST=AVL sanity and qualification tests passed and manual testing passed  Change-Id: I53d659a7962a2137fd922585881a189f8ac8e254 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304334 Commit-Ready: Ethan Ge &lt;ethan.ge@intel.com&gt; Commit-Ready: Tedd An &lt;tedd.an@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Ethan Ge &lt;ethan.ge@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Tedd An &lt;tedd.an@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ethan Ge &lt;ethan.ge@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Tedd An &lt;tedd.an@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Arman Uguray &lt;armansito@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304334" owner_email="tedd.an@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" ref="refs/changes/34/304334/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I5c09b78ffcc4c315ddc698a6e95b60174b7865b5" commit="fdc97b6f61440080dbb5d7cc484aafbb083abb08" commit_message="UPSTREAM: net/wireless: enable wiphy device to suspend/resume asynchronously  Now, PM core supports asynchronous suspend/resume mode for devices during system suspend/resume, and the power state transition of one device may be completed in separate kernel thread. PM core ensures all power state transition timing dependency between devices. This patch enables wiphy device to suspend/resume asynchronously. This can take advantage of multicore and improve system suspend/resume speed.  Comparison of power_Resume test results (by cywang): w/o patch seconds_system_resume_kernel{perf}=0.879189 seconds_system_resume{perf}=1.31215405464 w/ patch seconds_system_resume_kernel{perf}=0.634252 seconds_system_resume{perf}=1.07773995399  This shows an improvement of overall resume time of ~230 ms.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:46185 TEST=run the power_Resume test with and without this patch and check that the total wake-up time is shorter with this patch.  Change-Id: I5c09b78ffcc4c315ddc698a6e95b60174b7865b5 Signed-off-by: Zhonghui Fu &lt;zhonghui.fu@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg &lt;johannes.berg@intel.com&gt; (cherry-picked from 9f0e13546ef5773b7059b531a667ec47a5f897ee) Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/304591 Reviewed-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="304591" owner_email="luciano.coelho@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/304591/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I163ad23b2e782cc6e4fa41357b6fbca65ea3d846" commit="17ff12a9c10f87f638453159b8797cf01131620e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau/clk: GM20B: add debugfs gpu_edp_limit for gpu edp  Add debugfs interface gpu_edp_limit to show the limitted frequency.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:39762 TEST=cat /d/gpu_edp/gpu_edp_limit  Change-Id: I163ad23b2e782cc6e4fa41357b6fbca65ea3d846 Signed-off-by: Wei Ni &lt;wni@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303820 Commit-Ready: Puneet Kumar &lt;puneetster@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei Ni &lt;wni.nvidia@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Puneet Kumar &lt;puneetster@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303820" owner_email="wni.nvidia@gmail.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/303820/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1a817d4f5bc48b056b0fcbb0bb79adcea6c0fa5d" commit="c74edb43408f5c42e27fbd07198dfeaa2d34d5cf" commit_message="CHROMIUM: soc/tegra: add debugfs cpu_edp_limit for cpu edp  Add debugfs interface cpu_edp_limit for cpu edp  BUG=chrome-os-partner:39762 TEST=cat /d/cpu_edp/cpu_edp_limit  Change-Id: I1a817d4f5bc48b056b0fcbb0bb79adcea6c0fa5d Signed-off-by: Wei Ni &lt;wni@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/303461 Commit-Ready: David Riley &lt;davidriley@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei Ni &lt;wni.nvidia@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Riley &lt;davidriley@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="303461" owner_email="wni.nvidia@gmail.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/61/303461/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7529.0